cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Citewatch: a VS Code extension that checks Zenodo and Citation File Format metadata before a software release"
message: >-
  If you use or build on this software, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Organokov
    given-names: Mukharbek
    email: mukharbek.organokov@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3093-3456"
repository-code: "https://github.com/kabartay/citewatch"
abstract: >-
  A Visual Studio Code extension for making research software citable through
  Zenodo's GitHub integration without surprises. It checks .zenodo.json and
  CITATION.cff as they are typed: required fields, Zenodo's licence vocabulary
  (queried live), ORCID check digits, DOI and date formats, and that every file
  states the same version. Mistakes that would make Zenodo silently drop a
  release's deposit are reported as errors. The status bar shows the concept DOI
  and the newest archived version, and turns amber when Zenodo's webhook is not
  installed on the repository, so a release is not published without its DOI. It
  copies the DOI and a badge that is safe in a VS Code extension's README, and
  sets one version across package.json, pyproject.toml, CITATION.cff and
  .zenodo.json. Read-only towards Zenodo and GitHub, with no runtime dependencies
  and no telemetry. Unofficial; not affiliated with Zenodo, CERN or GitHub.
keywords:
  - Zenodo
  - Citation File Format
  - DOI
  - research software
  - Visual Studio Code extension
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-09"
